Feature: Radio shadows
  A tower that a team holds blocks the radio of the enemy. The [[radio shadow]] of a tower is
  all the ground and the air within its radio range, at all heights. [[Kinds of tower]] says how far that is for each kind. A drone in the radio shadow of
  an enemy tower is out of contact with its team. A tower that nobody holds, and a tower of the
  own team, block no radio.

  A drone out of contact sends no telemetry and no camera picture. It gets no new order. It
  flies the order that it had. If it is out of contact for 45 s, its link is lost. It then flies
  home by itself, and it stays on that order until the team can give it a new one.

  In the sim, the simulated air drops the frames of a drone in a radio shadow. In the field there is
  no such air, so the link has a filter: it knows who holds the towers and where the drones are, and
  it drops the frames that the rule says are lost. It is the same rule on both platforms.

  Expectation: A tower that a team holds blocks the radio of the enemy
    Given the Red home tower is held by Red
    And the first Blue drone is near the Red home tower
    Then the link of the first Blue drone is cut

  Expectation: A tower that nobody holds blocks no radio
    Given the Red home tower is neutral
    And the first Blue drone is near the Red home tower
    Then the link of the first Blue drone is in contact

  Expectation: A tower does not block the radio of its own team
    Given the first Blue drone is at the Blue home tower
    Then the link of the first Blue drone is in contact

  Expectation: A drone that leaves the radio shadow is in contact again
    Overrides: A tower that a team holds blocks the radio of the enemy
    Overrides: The filter of the link drops the frames of a drone in a radio shadow
    The tower still blocks the radio, but the drone is not in its shadow now.

    Given the Red home tower is held by Red
    And the first Blue drone is near the Red home tower
    When the first Blue drone flies out of the radio shadow
    Then the link of the first Blue drone is in contact

  Expectation: A drone that stays in the radio shadow for a short time is out of contact
    Given the Red home tower is held by Red
    And the first Blue drone is near the Red home tower
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the link of the first Blue drone is cut

  Expectation: A drone that stays in the radio shadow for 45 s loses its link
    Overrides: A tower that a team holds blocks the radio of the enemy
    After 45 s the link is lost, and not only cut.

    Given the Red home tower is held by Red
    And the first Blue drone is near the Red home tower
    When the game runs for 45 seconds
    Then the link of the first Blue drone is lost

  Expectation: The map keeps a drone out of contact where its team last heard from it
    Given the first Blue drone is low in the mid lane
    When the first Blue drone flies into the radio shadow for 10 seconds
    Then the first Blue drone on the Blue map is last in contact
    And the age of the first Blue drone on the Blue map is 10 s

  Expectation: A drone out of contact shows nothing of the enemy to its team
    Given the Red home tower is held by Red
    And the first Blue drone is near the Red home tower
    And the Red scout is 50 m from the first Blue drone
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the Red scout on the Blue map is unknown

  Expectation: A drone in contact shows the enemy near it to its team
    Given the Red home tower is neutral
    And the first Blue drone is near the Red home tower
    And the Red scout is 50 m from the first Blue drone
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the Red scout on the Blue map is seen

  Expectation: The computer commander gives no order to a drone out of contact
    Overrides: At the start, the commander sends a drone to each neutral tower
    The other drones get their orders as before.

    Given the Red home tower is held by Red
    And the first Blue drone is near the Red home tower
    When the computer commander of Blue decides
    Then the order of the first Blue drone is none

  Expectation: The filter of the link drops the frames of a drone in a radio shadow
    Given the Red home tower is held by Red
    And the first Blue drone is near the Red home tower
    Then the link filter lets the frames of the first Blue drone through is no

  Expectation: The filter of the link passes the frames of a drone in contact
    Overrides: The filter of the link drops the frames of a drone in a radio shadow
    Given the Red home tower is held by Red
    And the first Blue drone is at the Blue home tower
    Then the link filter lets the frames of the first Blue drone through is yes

  Expectation: The filter of the link passes the frames of a drone that a friend relays
    Overrides: The filter of the link drops the frames of a drone in a radio shadow
    Given the Red home tower is held by Red
    And the first Blue drone is 150 m from the Red home tower
    And the second Blue drone is 210 m from the Red home tower
    Then the link filter lets the frames of the first Blue drone through is yes
